{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Jxh5N1mG9ReCBWBQ8FiSDX","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t//! Translation of `quic/internal.h`.\n2\t//!\n3\t//! quic-core's grand internal header.  Anything that is not\n4\t//! part of the published `quic.h` API but is shared between\n5\t//! `.c` files of the core library lives here: connection /\n6\t//! path / stream / packet structures, frame and packet-type\n7\t//! enums, the giant `Quic` and `Connection`\n8\t//! structures that pin the rest of the library together, and\n9\t//! the long internal-only function surface (~200 functions).\n10\t//!\n11\t//! Phase 4: all function bodies have been filled in.\n12\t//!\n13\t//! Translation policy notes for this module:\n14\t//!\n15\t//! * Single-bit `unsigned int x : 1` bitfields collapse to\n16\t//!   `bool` per field (the \"ordinary integer field with\n17\t//!   mask/shift accessors\" rule, simplified for the trivial\n18\t//!   1-bit case where `bool` is clearer than `u32` + masks).\n19\t//! * Phase 1B replaced the C intrusive linked-list / splay /\n20\t//!   hash linkage with arena tokens\n21\t//!   ([`crate::arena::Token`], [`crate::splay::SplayToken`],\n22\t//!   [`crate::hash::HashToken`]).  Every per-collection\n23\t//!   membership is `Option<Token>` on the parent struct; the\n24\t//!   container holds the slot storage.  Zero raw pointers, no\n25\t//!   `unsafe`.\n26\t//! * The C `void* tls_master_ctx`, `void* aead_*`,\n27\t//!   `void* pn_enc/dec`, etc. were external-library handles\n28\t//!   ((picotls, OpenSSL).  Phase 2 replaced them with the\n29\t//!   trait family in [`crate::tls`] (`Session`, `PacketKey`,\n30\t//!   `HeaderKey`, …); backends supply implementations.\n31\t//! * `FILE* F_log` / `FILE* f_binlog` became\n32\t//!   `Option<std::fs::File>` in Phase 1B.\n33\t//! * `struct sockaddr_storage` fields fold into\n34\t//!   [`core::net::SocketAddr`].  Fields that the C code zeros out\n35\t//!   to mean \"address absent\" become `Option<SocketAddr>`.\n36\t//! * `Quic`, `Connection`, `Path` were\n37\t//!   forward-declared as opaque handles in\n38\t//!   [`crate`] (the public header).  Their\n39\t//!   real bodies live here; the public module re-exports the\n40\t//!   names so existing `use` paths in other modules keep\n41\t//!   working.\n42\t//! * Function pointer typedefs (`autoqlog_fn`,\n43\t//!   `performance_log_fn`, the spin-bit pair, the\n44\t//!   memlog hook on a connection, `mask_fns_t`) collapse to\n45\t//!   traits per the project rule.  When two function pointers\n46\t//!   are always installed together (`SpinbitDef`,\n47\t//!   `mask_fns_t`) they share one trait.\n48\t//! * Conditional fields gated by `BBRExperiment` and\n49\t//!   `WITH_THREAD_CHECK` are dropped — they are not\n50\t//!   part of the v1 target build.\n51\t//! * The `PARSE_*`/`IS_*_STREAM_ID(_*)` macros that the C\n52\t//!   header inlines as preprocessor macros are translated to\n53\t//!   `pub const fn` helpers.\n54\t\n55\tuse std::collections::{BTreeMap, VecDeque};\n56\tuse std::fs::File;\n57\tuse std::io::{Read, Write};\n58\tuse std::path::PathBuf;\n59\t\n60\tuse core::any::Any;\n61\tuse core::net::SocketAddr;\n62\t\n63\tuse crate::arena::{Arena, Token};\n64\tuse crate::hash::{HashTable, HashToken};\n65\tuse crate::splay::{SplayToken, SplayTree};\n66\tuse crate::{Duration, Instant};\n67\t\n68\t/// Token into the per-`Quic` connection arena.\n69\t///\n70\t/// Phase 4 plan: every C `*mut picoquic_cnx_t` becomes a\n71\t/// [`ConnectionToken`].  Following it requires `quic.connections.get(tok)`\n72\t/// — one indirection through the arena, plus a generation check.\n73\t/// Stable across operations on other connections.\n74\tpub type ConnectionToken = Token<Connection>;\n75\t\n76\t/// Token into the per-`Quic` registered-token replay-protection arena.\n77\tpub type RegisteredTokenToken = Token<RegisteredToken>;\n78\t\n79\t/// Token into the per-`Quic` issued-tickets arena (server-side replay state).\n80\tpub type IssuedTicketToken = Token<IssuedTicket>;\n81\t\n82\t/// Token into the per-`Connection` (or per-`StreamHead`) stream-related\n83\t/// arenas.  Phase 4 may further split these into per-collection types.\n84\tpub type StreamToken = Token<StreamHead>;\n85\tpub type StreamDataToken = Token<StreamDataNode>;\n86\tpub type PacketToken = Token<Packet>;\n87\tpub type SackItemToken = Token<SackItem>;\n88\tpub type LocalConnectionIdToken = Token<LocalConnectionId>;\n89\tpub type PathToken = Token<Path>;\n90\tuse crate::logger::LoggerRef;\n91\tuse crate::{\n92\t    AlpnSelect, CongestionAlgorithm, ConnectionId, ConnectionIdCallback, Fuzz, LossbitVersion,\n93\t    PacketContext, PathStatus, PmtudPolicy, RESET_SECRET_SIZE, SpinbitVersion, State,\n94\t    StreamDataCallback, StreamDirectReceive, TransportParameters,\n95\t};\n96\t\n97\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n98\t// Tunable constants (the `#define`s at the top of the C header).\n99\t\n100\tpub const MAX_PACKET_SIZE: usize = 1536;\n101\tpub const MIN_SEGMENT_SIZE: usize = 256;\n102\tpub const ENFORCED_INITIAL_MTU: usize = 1200;\n103\tpub const ENFORCED_INITIAL_CID_LENGTH: u8 = 8;\n104\tpub const PRACTICAL_MAX_MTU: usize = 1440;\n105\tpub const MIN_STREAM_DATA_FRAGMENT: usize = 512;\n106\tpub const RETRY_SECRET_SIZE: usize = 64;\n107\tpub const RETRY_TOKEN_PAD_SIZE: usize = 26;\n108\tpub const DEFAULT_0RTT_WINDOW: usize = 10 * ENFORCED_INITIAL_MTU;\n109\tpub const NB_PATH_TARGET: usize = 8;\n110\tpub const NB_PATH_DEFAULT: usize = 2;\n111\tpub const MAX_PACKETS_IN_POOL: i32 = 0x2000;\n112\tpub const INITIAL_FLOW_CONTROL_MAX: u64 = 0x100000;\n113\t\n114\tpub const INITIAL_RTT: Duration = Duration::from_ticks(250_000);\n115\tpub const TARGET_RENO_RTT: Duration = Duration::from_ticks(100_000);\n116\tpub const TARGET_SATELLITE_RTT: Duration = Duration::from_ticks(610_000);\n117\tpub const INITIAL_RETRANSMIT_TIMER: Duration = Duration::from_ticks(250_000);\n118\tpub const INITIAL_MAX_RETRANSMIT_TIMER: Duration = Duration::from_ticks(1_000_000);\n119\tpub const LARGE_RETRANSMIT_TIMER: Duration = Duration::from_ticks(2_000_000);\n120\tpub const MIN_RETRANSMIT_TIMER: Duration = Duration::from_ticks(50_000);\n121\tpub const ACK_DELAY_MAX: Duration = Duration::from_ticks(10_000);\n122\tpub const ACK_DELAY_MAX_DEFAULT: Duration = Duration::from_ticks(25_000);\n123\tpub const ACK_DELAY_MIN: Duration = Duration::from_ticks(1_000);\n124\tpub const ACK_DELAY_MIN_MAX_VALUE: u64 = 0xFFFFFF;\n125\tpub const RACK_DELAY: Duration = Duration::from_ticks(10_000);\n126\tpub const MAX_ACK_DELAY_MAX_MS: u64 = 0x4000;\n127\tpub const TOKEN_DELAY_LONG: Duration = Duration::from_ticks(24 * 60 * 60 * 1_000_000);\n128\tpub const TOKEN_DELAY_SHORT: Duration = Duration::from_ticks(2 * 60 * 1_000_000);\n129\tpub const CID_REFRESH_DELAY: Duration = Duration::from_ticks(5 * 1_000_000);\n130\tpub const MTU_LOSS_THRESHOLD: u64 = 10;\n131\t\n132\tpub const BANDWIDTH_ESTIMATE_MAX: u64 = 10_000_000_000;\n133\tpub const BANDWIDTH_TIME_INTERVAL_MIN: u64 = 1000;\n134\tpub const BANDWIDTH_MEDIUM: u64 = 2_000_000;\n135\tpub const MAX_BANDWIDTH_TIME_INTERVAL_MIN: u64 = 1000;\n136\tpub const MAX_BANDWIDTH_TIME_INTERVAL_MAX: u64 = 15000;\n137\t\n138\tpub const MINRTT_MARGIN: u64 = 128;\n139\tpub const MINRTT_THRESHOLD: u64 = 128;\n140\t\n141\tpub const SPURIOUS_RETRANSMIT_DELAY_MAX: Duration = Duration::from_ticks(1_000_000);\n142\t\n143\tpub const MICROSEC_SILENCE_MAX: Duration = Duration::from_ticks(120_000_000);\n144\tpub const MICROSEC_HANDSHAKE_MAX: Duration = Duration::from_ticks(30_000_000);\n145\tpub const MICROSEC_WAIT_MAX: Duration = Duration::from_ticks(10_000_000);\n146\t\n147\tpub const MICROSEC_STATELESS_RESET_INTERVAL_DEFAULT: Duration = Duration::from_ticks(100_000);\n148\t\n149\tpub const CWIN_INITIAL: u64 = 10 * MAX_PACKET_SIZE as u64;\n150\tpub const CWIN_MINIMUM: u64 = 2 * MAX_PACKET_SIZE as u64;"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"336f6a29-aee9-490b-87cc-680